{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Kinda_braindead)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Kinda braindead)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd5eaa48b2c8e2511c5463aa85f6dacc5b9c409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,b_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248c7fce7505e170b6baa31d38213068827399f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_2,b_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee81300e660fbfdc2150c399f2553a39482e3b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_3,b_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" /> of points in the coordinate plane satisfies\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bde321fe862959cb6e1121e2cf12bffc55bd6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n + 1}, b_{n + 1}) = (\\sqrt {3}a_n - b_n, \\sqrt {3}b_n + a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"300\" height=\"21\" />  for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9504173b0a7b5116af28352e278634eafcef83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1,2,3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c80629fe21d1e554ebd8acf920ab3f9355a25f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100}) = (2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11acdf75774ae941a2024408840e633e4f4eace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29de5d77fe5b0676f7f2e46147008cb0db0ce861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ -\\frac{1}{2^{97}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ -\\frac{1}{2^{99}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2^{98}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"457\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This sequence can also be expressed using matrix multiplication as follows: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8145c3c2d40b98971d259f7fefb379aaf5fea0fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[ \\begin{array}{c} a_{n+1} \\\\ b_{n+1} \\end{array} \\right] = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc} \\sqrt{3} &amp; -1 \\\\ 1 &amp; \\sqrt{3} \\end{array} \\right] \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} a_{n} \\\\ b_{n} \\end{array} \\right] = 2 \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc} \\cos 30^\\circ &amp; -\\sin 30^\\circ \\\\ \\sin 30^\\circ &amp; \\ \\cos 30^\\circ \\end{array} \\right] \\left[ \\begin{array}{c} a_{n} \\\\ b_{n} \\end{array} \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"515\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/49329d3a32f52ad960c2396d11bb9906793df7d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n+1} , b_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> is formed by rotating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3dfa275d1b489f988d3e46fddc8a992b02438e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n , b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> counter-clockwise about the origin by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and dilating the point's position with respect to the origin by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>So, starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a83ddcdda3f888e11d8b786ea13f4e093930d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and performing the above operations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times in reverse yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd5eaa48b2c8e2511c5463aa85f6dacc5b9c409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,b_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Rotating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f4d1e83d6eef61f31d78844deb189c54a7abc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> clockwise by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f80cee9f534e9817e788783274ead0f4e34d677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99 \\cdot 30^\\circ \\equiv 90^\\circ$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043b3c9c08690a58e011eb238316a58295360bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. A dilation by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e301b2f9e794a850cab75d3ce3fc56d53c2c384b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" /> yields the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e425203dfa45b4aea0761d8250b1b3f55d2267df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,b_1) = \\left(\\frac{4}{2^{99}}, -\\frac{2}{2^{99}} \\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{2^{97}}, -\\frac{1}{2^{98}} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"305\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdd28743082dfb41dbda2c2ffca311e6f42e4e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + b_1 = \\frac{1}{2^{97}} - \\frac{1}{2^{98}} = \\frac{1}{2^{98}} \\Rightarrow D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"250\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(algebra)\">Solution 2 (algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd11fcb5d00e49f42557398c545ec400778f32b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)=(a_1,b_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. Then, we can begin to list out terms as follows:\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98cfb5bd6d0ef80d4a5223d321ccd74c7d9b5d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_2,b_2)=(x\\sqrt{3}-y,y\\sqrt{3}+x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e394b8a7bde82fd65617076b21e358c165ee6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_3,b_3)=(2x-2y\\sqrt{3},2y+2x\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc895455b5fdd7dbeb2df6550e9e2caf9eb61541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_4,b_4)=(-8y,8x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>We notice that the sequence follows the rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/998e71354b5323f74393b47bd9a3e45b828b5590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n+3},b_{n+3})=(-2^3b_n,2^3a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We can now start listing out every third point, getting:\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55aec020d9adc6af2cb89d75b89f8313cec8408a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,b_1)=(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed343d62631c6ab0d2a4984af97732167b62658e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_4,b_4)=(-2^3y,2^3x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e8cf43805b0df8694d6a8e2eec9f1dcf680a6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_7,b_7)=(-2^6x,-2^6y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bf88abfdfe5234a7373260871e33c26a63b9e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{10},b_{10})=(2^9y,-2^9x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4376b2163c8c441ff1280b29422f06b8ec6a25d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{13},b_{13})=(2^{12}x,2^{12}y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>We can make two observations from this: \n</p><p>(1) In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" />, the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>(2) The positioning of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and their signs, cycle with every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>We know then that from (1), the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a83ddcdda3f888e11d8b786ea13f4e093930d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35feb15975e2851bfb307c36d66381c6e994ec94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{99}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can apply (2), finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e11d412dd444b65b762cb23ad3eb470e54eb921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\text{(mod }12)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />, so the positions and signs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are the same in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a83ddcdda3f888e11d8b786ea13f4e093930d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> as they are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe96d5b992ff949f4ad56edd4006e98fa409414a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{4},b_{4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>From this, we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e742f6026eb44cf7da6aa54b62a8ae25a53c024.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})=(-2^{99}y,2^{99}x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"19\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a630eb3a1aa0a3424523f7f782acd4a6425bad17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})=(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />, so we get the following:\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee313e9f2fc5a8888f0c361bf0c0e7bbee40308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2^{99}y=2 \\Rightarrow y=-\\frac{1}{2^{98}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"182\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b301222f4466567d7c6967fe95596e71e66ac9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{99}x=4 \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1}{2^{97}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"155\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1c0c52fbaaa7c534700df68e497c55f55fe5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=\\frac{1}{2^{97}}-\\frac{1}{2^{98}}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{2^{98}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"242\" height=\"48\" />..\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ordered pairs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />'s makes us think to use complex numbers. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8e5ff2f4757a50657462b8738c0a14a341ac8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n+1},b_{n+1}) = 2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}a_n - \\frac{1}{2}b_n, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}b_n + \\frac{1}{2}a_n\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"364\" height=\"55\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e0082052834ac130fa00ab4987e878e72a056d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} + b_{n+1}i = 2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}i\\right)(a_n + b_ni) = \\frac{1}{2}e^{i\\pi/6}(a_n + b_ni)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"466\" height=\"55\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3cac93ca363935933679c2c30bfc13f7168781e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n = a_n + b_ni$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f13e3cab2f9842ee2deb1247389961c832d78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{n+1} = a_{n+1} + b_{n+1}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d4746b93f123d915cb39177446b1597e1587cf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{n+1} = 2e^{i\\pi/6}z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e946518e0a3fe00764299ac0ae8dfab4b3fbb8f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\rightarrow n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede3442ce7f746d2b9dfada4047ebbe1cf023cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n = 2e^{i\\pi/6}z_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"22\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54b2167c023ce26b857fc42b4ba30952406b619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{n-1} = \\frac{1}{2}e^{-i\\pi/6}z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" />. This is the reverse transformation. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49cdc418ee1dfd695091d5e6ba4ff7b7e207e89e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{99} = \\frac{1}{2}e^{-i\\pi/6}z_{100}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/8519ded7a27223f4f56691c7b8a5145d412c6aa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{98} = \\frac{1}{2^2}e^{2(-i\\pi/6)}z_{100}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/76403adfdd35fb846675aaeaac92daec680a4fba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\vdots\\]\" width=\"2\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c323435e158b5c861b51a463e031d1f7ba77c1b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{1} = \\frac{1}{2^{99}}e^{99(-i\\pi/6)}z_{100}\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11b1ccdd637ed459e020abbb34f8f877d359a08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2^{99}}e^{-i\\pi/2}z_{100} = -\\frac{1}{2^{99}}i(2 + 4i) = \\frac{1}{2^{97}} - \\frac{1}{2^{98}}i.\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21b8732027d996814d73a0d3d0b578410f0ec13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + b_1 = \\frac{1}{2^{97}} - \\frac{1}{2^{98}} = \\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)}\\frac{1}{2^{98}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"250\" height=\"49\" /> ~ brainfertilzer.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Kinda_braindead.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Kinda_braindead)\">Solution 4 (Kinda braindead)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Kinda braindead)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by turning the two equations into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0bf8f8213ac38c610bd691071dfdeb5752f9d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = \\frac{a_{n+1}\\sqrt{3}+b_{n+1}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"164\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b37f7cc8034381efa0cc27ca5ddf10f09008429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\frac{b_{n+1}\\sqrt{3}-a_{n+1}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" />. Note that these are just obtained by solving the equations. \n</p><p><br />\nThis makes finding values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> much easier, and soon we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a6eb51ae0fa92e1f8ec753de79e0cbab4ea051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{97} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e890f847b9c9d0de7eb80c3256a19c4c2abbbc02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{97} = -\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />. After that, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0aae9533f923616c647ff8321cbc4da3f28fa0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{94} = -\\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c59b3db02b81a260b97d26acd9a17ca04ec654a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{94} = -\\frac{1}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdd3b81d3ff4c01dc870bff5d3b46b78ec9c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_n| = |\\frac{b_{n+3}}{8}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8dba732fd753128b3efae9c91065101b5ab3d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b_n| = |\\frac{a_{n+3}}{8}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"34\" />. This is basically just ignoring signs.\n</p><p><br />\nNow, we proceed to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdf72b7dbd7b9747bead76a19a632d98713959f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_1| = \\frac{1}{2^{97}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6964851db0958334a51345fa97ff679c0f403061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b_1| = \\frac{1}{2^{98}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. Despite there being 4 possible sign combinations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b6b5fa61a603351e622990b95e7d6dede017541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, b_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, the only achievable answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29127a5b850111e0e40d0f4fd5bf3cf857b5bbf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\frac{1}{2^{98}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\n-skibbysiggy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_4UJzyBslFA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_4UJzyBslFA</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A\">2008 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200146\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 517/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2264/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 162/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16567/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.834      1 -total\n 52.80%    8.361      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 45.68%    7.233      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!